BLISTER#VAMPIRE
AISLE#AGE#OILER
IN#YARN#NAPE#GO
LEG#MACHINE#SAD
IRON#GHOST#PALE
F#WEB#EGO#EON#N
FANCIER#NEGLECT
#W#KEG###ARE#U#
DESTROY#WRECKER
I#HIS#ASA#TAN#E
SHOE#ANKLE#TOLD
PEW#VIKINGS#BAR
ON#CERE#UGLY#TE
SNOUT#EAT#OASIS
EARBOBS#STEPINS


A1. What is often down at the heel? (Ask the girl who walks home.) ~ BLISTER
A7. What is "the other woman" called? ~ VAMPIRE
A13. What is the road to Matrimony? ~ AISLE
A14. Name something about a woman that keeps a man guessing. ~ AGE
A15. Who makes things run smoothly? ~ OILER
A16. Where does Maggie keep Jiggs when he wants to go out? ~ IN
A17. What did the gals of Grandma's day take for a spin? ~ YARN
A19. Name a part of the neck. ~ NAPE
A21. What would you do if you wanted to "beat it?" ~ GO
A22. What is being exposed a lot these days? ~ LEG
A24. What do you call the working organization of any political party? ~ MACHINE
A26. How did Romeo feel when Juliet went away? ~ SAD
A27. What do housewives do on Tuesday? ~ IRON
A29. Who spoke direful words to Hamlet? ~ GHOST
A30. What is a colorless individual? ~ PALE
A31. What is a spider's hangout? ~ WEB
A33. What is one's self? ~ EGO
A34. Name a period of time. ~ EON
A35. What do they call a person who breeds and sells animals and birds? ~ FANCIER
A38. What "sin of omission" causes many divorces? ~ NEGLECT
A41. What holds a lot of liquor? ~ KEG
A42. Name a part of the verb to be. ~ ARE
A43. What is a killing thing to do? ~ DESTROY
A46. What was Samson when he brought down the house? ~ WRECKER
A49. Name a masculine possessive pronoun. ~ HIS
A50. Who was champion of Jehovah against idolaters? ~ ASA
A52. What kind of coat did Huckleberry Finn wear to school? ~ TAN
A53. What is often underfoot? ~ SHOE
A55. What did the boys in 1895 often see on a rainy day? ~ ANKLE
A57. What did Benedict Arnold do? ~ TOLD
A59. What, in church, separates the sheep from the goats? ~ PEW
A60. What pirates ravaged the coasts of Europe from the 8th to 10th centuries? ~ VIKINGS
A62. At what is the line of the least resistance found? ~ BAR
A63. What word means "above and touching"? ~ ON
A64. What word means "to cover with wax"? ~ CERE
A65. What is an ill-natured disposition? ~ UGLY
A67. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ TE
A68. By what can you recognize a nosy reformer? ~ SNOUT
A70. What is a silly thing to do in night clubs? ~ EAT
A71. What is another name for a speakeasy? ~ OASIS
A73. What are often connected to receiving sets? (slang) ~ EARBOBS
A74. What do most girls like best—next to themselves? ~ STEPINS

D1. Name one who serves—unpleasantly. ~ BAILIFF
D2. What is a floating palace? ~ LINER
D3. Name a part of the verh "to be." ~ IS
D4. What kind of people make good reformers? ~ SLY
D5. What do ambitious college boys try to make? ~ TEAM
D6. Who makes money out of the wide open spaces? ~ RANCHER
D7. What is a deer thing to eat? ~ VENISON
D8. What do rejected calf-love suitors do? ~ MOPE
D9. What. weapon is frequently used in a Hollywood scrap? ~ PIE
D10. Name a French masculine pronoun. ~ IL
D11. What word describes the Courts of Royalty? ~ REGAL
D12. What medical word means "a caustic"? ~ ERODENT
D18. What is often chewed in public? ~ RAG
D20. Name a small social insect of the hymenopterous order. ~ ANT
D23. What often hangs around the ladies? ~ GOWN
D25. Name a famous rooter. ~ HOG
D26. What kind of men refuse to become crazy about women? ~ SANE
D28. What is the most colorful thing about vaudeville performers? ~ NECKTIE
D30. What kitty should only be fed at a distance? ~ POLECAT
D32. What are the last things in bunks? ~ BIERS
D34. Name a species of heron. ~ EGRET
D36. Name something in which many women keep their husbands. ~ AWE
D37. What is self-consciousness? ~ EGO
D39. What did Daniel Boone keep close to the ground? ~ EAR
D40. Name something seen in a Chinese poolroom. ~ CUE
D43. What word means "to distribute"? ~ DISPOSE
D44. What do flappers think their knees were made for? ~ SHOW
D45. Name an organization of famous N. Y. flyswatters. ~ YANKEES
D46. Name a species of squirrel food. ~ WALNUTS
D47. Name a round object fastened to doors and necks. ~ KNOB
D48. What does a gold-digger demand with her decree of divorce? ~ REDRESS
D51. Name a kind of slipper. ~ SKI
D54. What goes to the head of many girls? ~ HENNA
D55. What does many a windy person get? ~ AIR
D56. What was Humpty Dumpty? ~ EGG
D58. What kind of language did Nero use when he made it hot for the Romans? ~ LATIN
D60. What does Cal sometimes choose to do? ~ VETO
D61. Name a variety of wild, bitter plum. ~ SLOE
D64. What is a little bear? ~ CUB
D66. What is a doggy thing to do? ~ YAP
D69. Name a conjunction. ~ OR
D72. Name a Spanish affirmative. ~ SI


